e uh the developer um  have a nice  experience with with  with agni and and with creating  workflows  and and like testing distributed  application is something that is usually  very hard you'll need  lots of  shared components such as  data stores or a shared file system in  this example  even even kubernetes so what we did is  we kind of created a decoupling between  the workflow orchestration and the  creation of the workflow and the part of  the task execution themselves so  uh in production we could have kind of  plug and play for the same workflow you  could have kind of plug and play the  kubernetes executor making sure all the  tasks are being set to kubernetes uh and  for testing we could  use the same workflow plug and play the  the local executor and make uh and and  then the the task will be executed on  some local uh  process pool  so  of course we've kind of made a lot of  progress and and we still have lots of  ongoing challenges such as uh making the  scheduling much  much smarter  uh in the field of estimation of time  and resources  monitoring and visibility  dynamically changing  the workflows capping  helping the developer even  test their test their changes in a kind  of in a more production-grade  environment  and a lot more  and and just to to kind of wrap it up  uh we're now able to  utilize thousands of instances in the  cloud to support our many customers to  generate data at parallel we're talking  about thousands of data points in only a  few hours  and kind of help our customer train  better ai model just like we've kind of  promised at the beginning right  so  usually you'll see these kind of slides  i think in the beginning  um i thought to put it here  um but this is us this is datagen um our  customers are  tech giants from fortune 500 companies  from many verticals um and we are also  hiring so if any of this uh kind of  sounds interesting  please do uh uh contact me or  get into our website or whatever  so thank you  and  [Applause]
 

